<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bubastis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tell Basta, Per-Bast</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bubastis was a city in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a>, at Tell Basta near modern Zagazig, and the cult centre of the cat goddess Bastet. Libyan chiefs of the Meshwesh settled there, and their descendant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Shoshenq I</a> founded the Twenty-second Dynasty, whose kings enlarged its temple. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> described its festival of Bastet as the most popular in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and many mummified cats were buried in its cemeteries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bubastis.jpg" alt="Bubastis" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Einsamer Schütze · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bubastis_011.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
